# Chronus — Cursor Rules

This project uses **AGENTS.md** as the canonical instruction set for all AI
assistants (Hermes, Claude Code, Copilot, Cursor). The cursor rule files that
previously lived here have been removed because they duplicated, and in some
cases conflicted with, the AGENTS.md hierarchy.

## Read these files

Before writing or reviewing code, read the relevant AGENTS.md:

| Scope | File | What it covers |
|-------|------|----------------|
| Project-wide | `AGENTS.md` | Architecture, dependency rules, skills, pattern reference index |
| Backend | `backend/AGENTS.md` | Commands, pattern inventory, naming conventions, testing conventions, worked endpoint example |
| Frontend | `frontend/AGENTS.md` | Commands, MUI + CSS Modules styling, theme, routing, data fetching, worked page example |
| Migrations | `CLAUDE.md` | Migration naming conventions, backend module structure |
| Frontend (Claude) | `frontend/CLAUDE.md` | Frontend quick reference |
| Copilot | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` | Pointer to AGENTS.md |

## Per-module context

Each backend domain module has its own `AGENTS.md` under
`backend/src/{module}/AGENTS.md` listing its actions, services, transaction
scripts, aggregators, ports, entities, repositories, and folder structure.

## Pattern reference

Full DDD pattern documentation (24 pages) is in `backend/docs/patterns/`.
Start with `backend/docs/patterns/design-philosophy.md` and
`backend/docs/patterns/dependency-hierarchy.md`.

## Rules summary

- Actions call Services only; Services orchestrate Transaction Scripts
- No same-level injection (TS can't inject TS, Converter can't inject Converter)
- Blackbox principle: if A uses B and B uses C, A uses only B
- Cross-domain via Aggregators + ports, never direct entity references
- Domain output = Projections, not DTOs (no "Dto" in domain layer)
- Tests in `__specs__/` next to subject, SUT named `target`, Arrange-Act-Assert
- Frontend: MUI `sx` + CSS Modules, no Tailwind, React Query for data fetching
